First install the DNS Service;
  1.server manager
  2.manage
  3.roles and features
  4.click on next
  5.check role based and feature based installation
  6.select the host name (eg. master.itiss.com) 
  7.check the DNS server 
  8.in pop up add features and click on next
  9.click on next 
  10.check restart option
  11.install

Second Create lookup zones;

1.forward lookup zone and forward lookup record
  a)forward zone creation
  1.server manager
  2.tools
  3.dns
  4.click on our server name(eg. master)
  5.click on forward lookup zone 
  6.right click on forward lookup zone
  7.slect new zone
  8.next 
  9.check primary zone
  10.give zone name (eg. itiss.com)
  11.check create file (select by default file name) and next
  12.check do not allow dynamic chnages and nnext
  13.finish
  b)forward zone record creation
  1.in forward zone
  2.select zone name (eg.itiss.com)
  3.right click on it and add (A,CNAME,MAX record)
  4.give fqdn(fully qualified domain name eg. master.itiss.com) and give ip address on which you want to resolve hostname
  5.add host
  
2.reverse lookup zone and reverse lookup record
  a)reverse zone creation
  1.server manager
  2.tools
  3.dns
  4.click on our server name(eg. master)
  5.click on reverse lookup zone 
  6.right click on reverse lookup zone
  7.slect new zone
  8.next 
  9.check primary zone
  10.check ipv4 and next
  11.give network ip
  12.check create file (select by default file name) and next
  13.check do not allow dynamic chnages and nnext
  14.finish
  b)reverse zone record creation
  1.in reverse zone
  2.select zone name (eg.given network id)
  3.right click on it and add (PTR record)
  4.give host ip or server ip (eg 192.168.238.100) and complete host name(eg. master.itiss.com)
  5.add ptr

Third verify dns;
  nslookup given_domain_name or ip_address
  eg.nslookup master.itiss.com
  eg.nslookup itiss.com
  eg.nslookup 192.168.238.100
  
  

  
